WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.185
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:17.455 --> 00:18.455
Dear.

3
00:20.037 --> 00:20.783
Den!

4
00:20.842 --> 00:21.842
Dear.

5
00:23.866 --> 00:24.581
Help me.

6
00:24.888 --> 00:26.029
Den, where are you?

7
00:27.760 --> 00:28.890
I'm trapped in here.

8
00:29.020 --> 00:30.020
Den!

9
00:31.938 --> 00:33.909
I'm here. Den, where are you?

10
00:34.685 --> 00:35.685
Dear.

11
00:36.689 --> 00:38.151
Den, I'm here.

12
00:40.057 --> 00:41.057
Dear.

13
00:43.902 --> 00:44.902
Dear.

14
00:45.826 --> 00:46.826
Den.

15
00:50.063 --> 00:51.063
Den.

16
01:06.627 --> 01:07.627
Dear.

17
01:08.305 --> 01:08.670
Dear.

18
01:08.847 --> 01:09.847
Den.

19
01:09.969 --> 01:10.348
Den.

20
01:10.648 --> 01:11.648
Dear, help me.

21
01:13.174 --> 01:13.690
Den.

22
01:13.853 --> 01:14.853
Blood.

23
01:21.915 --> 01:23.293
I'm here, Den.

24
01:33.600 --> 01:34.600
Den!

25
01:53.489 --> 01:54.489
Who's there?

26
01:54.918 --> 01:56.700
I'm here to make a delivery.

27
02:22.576 --> 02:23.576
What are you doing here?

28
02:24.580 --> 02:26.668
It's my day off, so I thought I'd drop by.

29
02:28.581 --> 02:29.581
And...

30
02:30.398 --> 02:31.398
What's this?

31
02:33.923 --> 02:34.923
I got it for you.

32
02:46.661 --> 02:48.939
Have you always lived alone, Dear?

33
02:51.909 --> 02:52.909
Yeah.

34
02:53.057 --> 02:54.558
That must get lonely.

35
02:56.210 --> 02:57.210
I'm used to it.

36
03:00.106 --> 03:02.026
Being used to it doesn't mean you're not lonely.

37
03:05.016 --> 03:07.210
So... you came here to keep me company?

38
03:11.015 --> 03:11.407
Yeah.

39
03:11.981 --> 03:12.981
Something like that.

40
03:24.293 --> 03:26.069
You remembered I like it less sweet.

41
03:26.297 --> 03:27.297
Well?

42
03:27.518 --> 03:28.678
Pretty thoughtful of me, huh?

43
03:42.523 --> 03:43.523
What are you staring at?

44
03:45.317 --> 03:46.317
Nothing.

45
03:48.052 --> 03:49.052
Thanks.

46
03:55.239 --> 03:56.822
Then I'm staying for a while today.

47
03:58.822 --> 03:59.938
Who said you could?

48
04:01.081 --> 04:02.081
Well...

49
04:02.295 --> 04:03.966
You already took the milk tea.

50
04:04.246 --> 04:05.408
So you owe me one.

51
04:08.987 --> 04:10.874
Is this any good? Is it?

52
05:14.126 --> 05:15.126
Hello.

53
05:17.501 --> 05:19.738
I'm only half an hour late. Don't hold it against me.

54
05:21.378 --> 05:22.378
Nava's asleep.

55
05:22.845 --> 05:24.624
You can wait outside the room and keep watch.

56
05:24.648 --> 05:25.648
Oh.

57
05:25.966 --> 05:26.966
Sure.

58
05:34.660 --> 05:35.660
Here you go.

59
05:40.731 --> 05:41.573
You should get to work.

60
05:41.676 --> 05:43.510
Don't worry about Nava. I'll look after her.

61
05:44.752 --> 05:45.752
Okay.

62
06:20.240 --> 06:21.760
Aren't you going in? You'll be late.

63
06:45.361 --> 06:46.361
Don't worry.

64
06:46.943 --> 06:48.663
I don't think anything will happen tonight.

65
06:51.009 --> 06:52.530
When the lights turn blue,

66
06:52.531 --> 06:54.571
it means the period is safe.

67
06:54.834 --> 06:57.628
No customers will enter the store during this time.

68
06:58.294 --> 06:59.488
It's really safe, right?

69
07:04.461 --> 07:05.461
Yeah.

70
07:05.936 --> 07:07.379
Usually, nothing happens.

71
07:08.345 --> 07:09.345
But in the past...

72
07:10.309 --> 07:12.555
these blue lights came on even more often.

73
07:17.817 --> 07:19.057
It’s the quiet nights like this

74
07:20.532 --> 07:21.532
that are scarier.

75
07:21.981 --> 07:22.981
Scarier?

76
07:25.264 --> 07:26.974
They make you paranoid.

77
07:28.191 --> 07:29.191
The less that happens,

78
07:31.089 --> 07:31.999
the more it feels like

79
07:32.023 --> 07:34.143
something could jump out and attack us at any moment.

80
07:41.021 --> 07:42.033
You're still here

81
07:43.965 --> 07:45.205
because of your brother, right?

82
07:57.365 --> 07:59.199
Den used to work the night shift here.

83
08:01.889 --> 08:02.933
Then one night...

84
08:04.304 --> 08:05.433
he never came back.

85
08:09.108 --> 08:10.413
I asked Cherd about it once,

86
08:12.070 --> 08:13.499
but all he said was...

87
08:16.317 --> 08:17.877
Den disappeared before his shift ended.

88
08:23.262 --> 08:24.262
In the end...

89
08:25.550 --> 08:26.816
I came to work here

90
08:28.990 --> 08:30.710
hoping I might find him or learn something.

91
08:31.483 --> 08:32.483
What if..

92
08:32.919 --> 08:33.919
You never find anything?

93
08:35.144 --> 08:37.331
Are you going to keep working here forever?

94
08:38.943 --> 08:40.007
Aren't you scared?

95
08:42.937 --> 08:44.380
I might have been scared before,

96
08:46.478 --> 08:47.633
but now I'm used to it.

97
08:49.813 --> 08:50.813
Trust me.

98
08:51.074 --> 08:52.154
You'll get used to it, too.

99
09:07.074 --> 09:08.914
Okay, this side's done. Give me the other one.

100
09:15.125 --> 09:16.125
What happened to you?

101
09:18.115 --> 09:19.115
Does it hurt?

102
09:23.509 --> 09:24.638
Nava, answer me.

103
09:50.328 --> 09:52.044
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

104
10:05.708 --> 10:06.708
Sergeant Wichian.

105
10:06.799 --> 10:07.204
Hey.

106
10:07.406 --> 10:07.967
Captain.

107
10:08.261 --> 10:09.261
What are you doing here?

108
10:10.220 --> 10:12.236
Oh, I've resigned from the police force.

109
10:12.491 --> 10:12.863
What?

110
10:13.385 --> 10:14.385
Why?

111
10:15.043 --> 10:16.401
Some family problems, sir.

112
10:17.302 --> 10:19.266
And now you're working at a store?

113
10:23.599 --> 10:24.337
All right.

114
10:24.618 --> 10:25.938
I don't mean to look down on you.

115
10:27.437 --> 10:28.978
Leaving the police force

116
10:29.389 --> 10:30.469
might even be for the best.

117
10:31.373 --> 10:32.476
Good cops

118
10:33.553 --> 10:34.553
die young.

119
10:37.801 --> 10:38.801
Your change is five baht.

120
10:41.509 --> 10:42.509
I'd better go.

121
10:43.331 --> 10:44.731
I have to keep patrolling the area.

122
10:48.519 --> 10:50.018
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

123
10:57.900 --> 10:59.123
You've been working here for a week now.

124
10:59.147 --> 11:00.147
How do you feel?

125
11:20.612 --> 11:22.694
Tell me how many cans you want. I'll get them.

126
11:26.892 --> 11:27.892
It's getting better.

127
11:28.941 --> 11:30.581
I don't get startled as easily as before.

128
11:34.992 --> 11:35.632
Excuse me.

129
11:35.919 --> 11:36.311
Yes?

130
11:36.559 --> 11:38.058
One bag of porridge for a kid, please.

131
11:38.082 --> 11:39.191
Sure, coming right up.

132
11:39.882 --> 11:40.882
Hey.

133
11:41.311 --> 11:42.333
You don't live alone?

134
11:43.882 --> 11:44.352
No.

135
11:44.705 --> 11:45.945
Right, I live with my daughter.

136
11:46.141 --> 11:47.141
Seriously?

137
11:47.492 --> 11:48.492
You have a daughter?

138
11:52.101 --> 11:53.974
She's seven. Her name's Nava.

139
11:54.829 --> 11:55.829
What about her mother?

140
12:16.572 --> 12:17.212
Well...

141
12:17.525 --> 12:18.693
Why are you working here?

142
12:21.846 --> 12:22.846
Just what you guessed.

143
12:24.574 --> 12:25.574
I'm in debt,

144
12:26.507 --> 12:28.027
so I need to earn money to pay it off.

145
12:33.092 --> 12:34.092
Your porridge is ready.

146
12:34.471 --> 12:35.471
Thank you.

147
12:43.692 --> 12:44.692
Metha.

148
12:45.403 --> 12:46.403
Metha.

149
12:49.202 --> 12:50.202
What's up?

150
12:50.462 --> 12:51.462
Well...

151
12:52.569 --> 12:53.849
Do you still owe a lot of money?

152
12:55.213 --> 12:56.213
Why do you ask?

153
12:59.377 --> 13:00.591
If you need money,

154
13:01.972 --> 13:03.092
you can borrow some from me.

155
13:10.000 --> 13:11.626
How could I let a kid like you help me?

156
13:13.224 --> 13:14.236
I can handle it myself.

157
13:16.997 --> 13:17.997
But still...

158
13:18.694 --> 13:19.694
thanks.

159
13:35.757 --> 13:37.473
Oh, let me tell you.

160
13:37.617 --> 13:38.883
It's such a mess.

161
13:39.719 --> 13:40.783
Yeah, exactly.

162
13:41.011 --> 13:42.056
Poor kid.

163
13:42.347 --> 13:43.896
All she knows is that her mother ran away

164
13:43.920 --> 13:44.920
and abandoned her.

165
13:45.630 --> 13:47.314
I feel so sorry for her.

166
13:47.549 --> 13:49.664
I really do. She hardly speaks.

167
13:50.173 --> 13:50.735
It's like...

168
13:51.074 --> 13:51.772
what do you call it?

169
13:52.014 --> 13:53.744
Oh, a troubled child.

170
13:53.882 --> 13:55.494
One of those mentally disturbed kids.

171
13:55.814 --> 13:56.814
Yeah.

172
13:57.162 --> 13:59.183
I don't know how he manages it.

173
13:59.495 --> 14:02.465
Besides, he's not even the child's real father.

174
14:02.951 --> 14:04.603
Okay, I have to go.

175
14:05.700 --> 14:06.700
Oh.

176
14:06.855 --> 14:07.855
Metha.

177
14:08.386 --> 14:09.464
You're back.

178
14:10.981 --> 14:12.528
Nava's still asleep.

179
14:22.731 --> 14:24.441
What happened to the stuffed rabbit?

180
14:25.357 --> 14:25.690
Well...

181
14:26.134 --> 14:27.688
I thought it was old,

182
14:27.877 --> 14:30.357
so I was going to wash it, but Nava wouldn't let me.

183
14:38.620 --> 14:40.036
She really loves that rabbit.

184
14:42.275 --> 14:43.346
I understand that.

185
14:43.581 --> 14:46.452
But some things should be thrown away.

186
14:46.477 --> 14:47.308
They clutter up the house.

187
14:47.401 --> 14:48.830
Or you could donate it.

188
14:48.994 --> 14:50.034
That would be a good deed.

189
14:52.701 --> 14:53.701
Well...

190
14:53.987 --> 14:55.012
I'll head home now.

191
14:56.618 --> 14:57.618
Okay.

192
15:05.831 --> 15:08.237
Ta-da. Mr. Rabbit.

193
15:24.782 --> 15:25.782
Don't worry.

194
15:26.982 --> 15:28.320
I will get it fixed.

195
15:30.043 --> 15:31.329
It will be as good as new.

196
15:36.779 --> 15:40.669
(Arunchai School)

197
15:48.740 --> 15:50.335
Excuse me, Nava's father.

198
15:51.038 --> 15:52.918
There's something I'd like to discuss with you.

199
15:53.198 --> 15:54.608
Please come inside for a moment.

200
15:58.837 --> 16:00.462
I'd like to talk to you about Nava.

201
16:01.507 --> 16:02.721
From what I've observed,

202
16:03.380 --> 16:04.973
Nava is very quiet.

203
16:05.560 --> 16:06.560
Quite often,

204
16:07.016 --> 16:08.654
she keeps to herself.

205
16:09.830 --> 16:10.830
And...

206
16:11.398 --> 16:12.997
all she does is draw.

207
16:15.850 --> 16:16.940
I'm not sure

208
16:17.064 --> 16:20.412
whether something at home is making her stressed

209
16:20.772 --> 16:22.359
or upsetting her.

210
16:24.885 --> 16:27.195
She's been through a lot.

211
16:32.772 --> 16:34.372
But I'll try to take better care of her.

212
16:35.762 --> 16:36.762
Well...

213
16:36.969 --> 16:38.329
please take good care of her, sir.

214
16:40.527 --> 16:41.527
I will.

215
16:53.424 --> 16:54.488
So, about that case...

216
16:58.984 --> 17:00.250
the court has dismissed it.

217
17:04.996 --> 17:06.062
(Socialite Pruekpana cleared of charges)

218
17:06.086 --> 17:07.366
But you're not the one at fault.

219
17:13.664 --> 17:14.800
Don't blame yourself.

220
17:18.318 --> 17:19.318
Just let it go.

221
17:20.583 --> 17:21.663
You did the best you could.

222
17:24.083 --> 17:25.083
Did I?

223
17:27.973 --> 17:29.573
What about the victims who were scammed?

224
17:32.852 --> 17:33.972
What do you expect me to do?

225
17:34.530 --> 17:35.930
That's just how this country works.

226
17:37.291 --> 17:38.611
If you've got money, you get off.

227
17:42.413 --> 17:43.817
Have you signed for me?

228
17:46.545 --> 17:50.233
Pruek said he only needs a little more money.

229
17:51.319 --> 17:53.277
You know I'm finally getting somewhere.

230
17:54.687 --> 17:56.130
And this business

231
17:56.450 --> 17:57.697
could take us a long way.

232
18:02.348 --> 18:03.523
But this house...

233
18:03.862 --> 18:04.862
Honey.

234
18:06.604 --> 18:08.386
Do you trust me?

235
18:09.398 --> 18:10.918
I know it'll succeed

236
18:13.383 --> 18:14.656
if we work together.

237
18:19.729 --> 18:20.916
Trust me.

238
18:25.687 --> 18:26.687
All right.

239
18:27.691 --> 18:28.983
Yeah, thank you.

240
18:56.845 --> 18:58.731
That's an oddly designed stuffed animal.

241
18:59.266 --> 19:00.409
Oh, Cherd.

242
19:03.202 --> 19:05.046
(Manager Room)

243
19:09.890 --> 19:10.890
Are you tired?

244
19:11.528 --> 19:12.528
Yeah.

245
19:12.840 --> 19:13.840
Lately,

246
19:14.656 --> 19:16.516
we've been short on night-shift staff.

247
19:18.121 --> 19:20.242
New people join and leave soon after.

248
19:21.033 --> 19:22.217
It's hard to find replacements.

249
19:22.241 --> 19:23.429
No one's applying at all.

250
19:27.279 --> 19:28.447
But the pay is so good.

251
19:29.518 --> 19:31.038
It probably isn't hard to find people.

252
19:31.620 --> 19:32.762
You still don't know

253
19:33.350 --> 19:34.805
that not everyone can see

254
19:35.181 --> 19:36.501
the job ad?

255
19:40.483 --> 19:42.043
Especially for our store's night shift.

256
19:45.208 --> 19:46.560
Not everyone can see it?

257
19:46.938 --> 19:47.454
Yeah.

258
19:47.852 --> 19:48.852
That's right.

259
19:53.581 --> 19:54.581
This store

260
19:55.709 --> 19:56.709
chooses the people.

261
19:57.641 --> 19:58.641
Chooses them?

262
19:59.886 --> 20:00.886
How?

263
20:02.295 --> 20:04.513
What do you think this store really is?

264
20:08.403 --> 20:09.403
It's...

265
20:10.368 --> 20:12.281
a place that connects the world of the living

266
20:13.162 --> 20:14.454
to the world of the dead?

267
20:16.214 --> 20:17.226
Well...

268
20:18.277 --> 20:19.608
You could look at it that way.

269
20:20.196 --> 20:22.474
But I see this store as

270
20:23.120 --> 20:25.026
something like a convenience store

271
20:25.130 --> 20:26.703
for people who have died.

272
20:27.749 --> 20:29.351
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

273
20:29.451 --> 20:30.529
Actually, I don't think

274
20:31.077 --> 20:33.157
the dead are all that different from people like us.

275
20:33.205 --> 20:35.274
They miss the food they used to eat,

276
20:35.810 --> 20:37.853
the things they used to use,

277
20:38.568 --> 20:39.728
and when they want something,

278
20:39.857 --> 20:41.306
they stop by this store to buy it.

279
20:41.620 --> 20:43.343
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

280
20:43.486 --> 20:44.780
Or maybe

281
20:44.968 --> 20:46.228
they come back

282
20:47.525 --> 20:50.769
because there's something they can't let go of,

283
20:51.232 --> 20:52.498
something left unresolved.

284
20:55.817 --> 20:56.817
Something like that.

285
21:21.610 --> 21:22.708
Oh, Nava.

286
21:24.516 --> 21:26.703
I was only putting it away.

287
21:26.844 --> 21:28.244
I wasn't going to take it anywhere.

288
21:29.527 --> 21:30.871
He said he doesn't like it.

289
21:52.567 --> 21:53.567
That crazy kid

290
21:53.830 --> 21:56.027
gets stranger and stranger every day.

291
23:05.526 --> 23:06.526
That little weirdo.

292
23:15.712 --> 23:17.723
Ouch.

293
23:17.890 --> 23:19.499
Ouch. It hurts.

294
23:19.798 --> 23:20.470
It's me.

295
23:20.703 --> 23:21.703
Hey.

296
23:23.015 --> 23:24.015
Come on.

297
23:24.379 --> 23:25.379
Sorry.

298
23:25.622 --> 23:26.622
Good.

299
23:27.073 --> 23:28.073
When did you get here?

300
23:28.219 --> 23:29.366
Come on, bro.

301
23:29.504 --> 23:30.672
I've been here a while.

302
23:31.471 --> 23:33.226
Didn't you hear my car?

303
23:34.954 --> 23:35.535
Sorry.

304
23:35.962 --> 23:37.071
I got carried away.

305
23:39.530 --> 23:40.530
Carried away?

306
23:42.367 --> 23:43.367
I used to be a cop.

307
23:44.117 --> 23:45.962
Whoa, that's so cool.

308
23:46.090 --> 23:47.090
It's not cool.

309
23:47.925 --> 23:49.685
I'm just trying to make it through each day.

310
23:52.404 --> 23:53.404
Working here,

311
23:53.905 --> 23:55.471
just surviving is good enough, bro.

312
23:59.170 --> 24:00.370
Don't do that again. It hurts.

313
24:00.884 --> 24:01.884
Sorry.

314
24:09.323 --> 24:10.643
I've finished checking the stock.

315
24:10.870 --> 24:11.870
Anything else to do?

316
24:12.011 --> 24:13.011
I don't think so.

317
24:14.395 --> 24:16.902
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

318
24:33.997 --> 24:34.997
Metha.

319
24:44.548 --> 24:45.598
Why are you here?

320
24:46.292 --> 24:47.292
And...

321
24:48.751 --> 24:50.116
how's Nava doing?

322
24:54.082 --> 24:56.679
I know I left you and Nava, but...

323
24:57.762 --> 24:58.946
I didn't mean to.

324
25:01.648 --> 25:02.085
I...

325
25:02.266 --> 25:03.648
I really wanted to come see you.

326
25:04.656 --> 25:06.282
I've always wanted to come see you.

327
25:07.157 --> 25:08.693
I really wanted to, but...

328
25:09.093 --> 25:10.133
I didn't have the courage.

329
25:10.924 --> 25:11.924
I'm sorry.

330
25:12.788 --> 25:13.788
It's okay, Nam.

331
25:14.143 --> 25:15.263
You don't have to apologize.

332
25:15.423 --> 25:16.618
I'm sorry, Metha.

333
25:22.391 --> 25:23.391
Metha.

334
25:25.729 --> 25:26.119
Yeah?

335
25:26.689 --> 25:27.689
Is something wrong?

336
25:29.324 --> 25:30.324
She's someone I know.

337
25:32.630 --> 25:34.310
Can I step away and talk to her privately?

338
25:38.587 --> 25:39.587
Someone you know?

339
25:41.330 --> 25:42.770
There's something we need to settle.

340
25:43.092 --> 25:44.852
I don't want to disturb the other customers.

341
25:47.486 --> 25:48.486
Okay.

342
25:56.965 --> 25:58.778
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

343
25:58.826 --> 25:59.826
Hey!

344
25:59.866 --> 26:00.866
You.

345
26:01.807 --> 26:03.287
Hurry up and put the money in my bag!

346
26:04.828 --> 26:05.828
Move it!

347
26:09.933 --> 26:10.933
Hey.

348
26:11.778 --> 26:13.037
I said put the money in my bag!

349
26:14.733 --> 26:15.733
Hurry!

350
26:16.637 --> 26:17.213
Are you even human?

351
26:17.459 --> 26:19.760
Stop asking. Put the money in the bag now!

352
26:22.277 --> 26:23.277
I'll go get it.

353
26:23.717 --> 26:24.717
Hurry.

354
26:33.350 --> 26:34.350
You.

355
26:34.715 --> 26:35.835
What are you trying to pull?

356
26:41.068 --> 26:42.628
I told you to put the money in the bag!

357
26:42.705 --> 26:44.108
Or this woman dies!

358
26:44.796 --> 26:45.796
Now!

359
26:45.972 --> 26:46.972
Metha.

360
27:31.627 --> 27:34.032
I said put the money in the bag, or this woman dies!

361
27:34.323 --> 27:35.323
Hurry!

362
27:36.558 --> 27:36.958
Metha.

363
27:37.118 --> 27:37.571
Hurry up.

364
27:37.596 --> 27:37.947
Okay.

365
27:38.374 --> 27:38.672
Got it.

366
27:38.768 --> 27:39.768
Now!

367
27:39.862 --> 27:40.862
Dear, help me.

368
27:41.984 --> 27:42.984
Move it.

369
27:43.659 --> 27:44.921
Hurry up, man.

370
27:45.310 --> 27:46.310
I'll really shoot.

371
28:01.295 --> 28:02.345
What are you up to?

372
28:03.647 --> 28:04.671
Is this all you've got?

373
28:05.497 --> 28:06.497
You two,

374
28:06.567 --> 28:07.969
get away from the counter!

375
28:08.628 --> 28:09.628
I can't.

376
28:09.926 --> 28:11.006
What are you talking about?

377
28:14.742 --> 28:15.742
Store rules.

378
28:16.529 --> 28:17.345
The counter can't be left unattended

379
28:17.369 --> 28:18.489
for more than three minutes.

380
28:18.630 --> 28:20.305
I don't care about your stupid rules.

381
28:20.875 --> 28:21.905
I said back off!

382
28:23.622 --> 28:24.622
I'm counting to three.

383
28:26.756 --> 28:27.756
Alright.

384
28:28.260 --> 28:28.852
Move.

385
28:28.905 --> 28:29.905
Got it.

386
28:32.143 --> 28:32.721
Hurry up!

387
28:32.746 --> 28:33.746
I'm moving.

388
28:35.905 --> 28:37.142
Both of you, sit down.

389
28:38.113 --> 28:39.113
Now!

390
28:40.273 --> 28:41.745
Don't try anything funny.

391
28:42.102 --> 28:43.342
Come on. You're coming with me.

392
28:58.442 --> 29:00.308
What? That's all you've got?

393
29:04.659 --> 29:04.958
Hey.

394
29:05.668 --> 29:07.038
Metha, time's almost up.

395
29:07.062 --> 29:08.062
What's with these lights?

396
29:10.505 --> 29:11.505
I'll go.

397
29:15.641 --> 29:16.641
Hey!

398
29:17.688 --> 29:18.755
I told you not to move.

399
29:29.167 --> 29:31.252
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

400
29:32.249 --> 29:33.249
Put the gun down

401
29:33.740 --> 29:34.972
and release the hostage.

402
29:36.375 --> 29:37.655
You put your gun down.

403
29:38.567 --> 29:39.740
Or this woman dies!

404
29:40.199 --> 29:41.199
Hurry.

405
29:43.976 --> 29:45.139
Move it, old man.

406
29:46.296 --> 29:47.296
Put the gun down.

407
29:50.205 --> 29:51.205
Now!

408
30:03.814 --> 30:04.814
What's with these lights?

409
30:05.056 --> 30:06.056
Hey.

410
30:06.480 --> 30:07.480
What's going on?

411
30:17.376 --> 30:18.390
Hey, Captain.

412
30:19.190 --> 30:19.776
Oh, Sergeant.

413
30:20.041 --> 30:21.961
You're about to be promoted to inspector, right?

414
30:22.381 --> 30:23.381
Oh.

415
30:23.538 --> 30:24.698
I'm not quite there yet, sir.

416
30:25.800 --> 30:26.872
If not you, Captain,

417
30:27.346 --> 30:28.346
then who?

418
30:29.320 --> 30:31.256
I trained you myself.

419
30:33.162 --> 30:34.162
But it's a good thing.

420
30:34.586 --> 30:36.080
We're all getting old.

421
30:37.477 --> 30:38.544
We'll be retiring soon.

422
30:40.305 --> 30:42.652
Then we can relax and look after our grandkids.

423
30:49.400 --> 30:49.704
Here.

424
30:50.248 --> 30:51.248
My granddaughter.

425
30:52.152 --> 30:53.389
She was born just last week.

426
30:53.837 --> 30:54.837
Wow.

427
30:55.352 --> 30:56.352
She's cute, Sergeant.

428
30:57.240 --> 30:58.240
Congratulations.

429
30:58.841 --> 31:00.985
Prawet One, reporting incident 241.

430
31:01.353 --> 31:02.852
Location, Yaowarat Gold Shop.

431
31:03.049 --> 31:04.879
One armed suspect, unknown weapon.

432
31:04.932 --> 31:05.551
We've got a call.

433
31:05.631 --> 31:06.644
Units are on their way.

434
31:06.719 --> 31:07.719
Stop.

435
31:09.216 --> 31:10.696
Aren't your reports still unfinished?

436
31:12.298 --> 31:13.858
Let the experienced officers handle it.

437
31:14.331 --> 31:16.291
Save your energy for your promotion to inspector.

438
31:32.507 --> 31:32.864
Hey.

439
31:33.510 --> 31:34.672
Stop! Don't move!

440
31:35.659 --> 31:36.659
Drop your weapon!

441
31:37.222 --> 31:38.379
I said put the gun down.

442
31:38.704 --> 31:39.704
Or this woman dies!

443
31:39.973 --> 31:40.848
Release the hostage!

444
31:40.923 --> 31:41.712
Hurry up!

445
31:41.765 --> 31:42.683
You can't get away.

446
31:42.784 --> 31:43.784
Hurry!

447
31:43.867 --> 31:44.867
Put the gun down!

448
31:46.758 --> 31:47.758
Idiot.

449
32:02.296 --> 32:05.315
One officer has died at the scene.

450
32:05.678 --> 32:07.262
The suspect has now fled.

451
32:07.336 --> 32:09.351
Report any suspect immediately.

452
32:09.570 --> 32:10.719
The suspect is armed.

453
32:18.346 --> 32:19.346
Hey.

454
32:19.775 --> 32:20.775
What?

455
32:29.125 --> 32:30.125
Hey.

456
32:33.152 --> 32:34.309
Aren't you dead?

457
32:34.565 --> 32:36.421
You remember now?

458
32:37.329 --> 32:38.329
Go.

459
32:40.273 --> 32:41.273
Go.

460
32:41.798 --> 32:43.761
Using a hostage again, huh?

461
32:43.814 --> 32:44.814
Go.

462
32:44.913 --> 32:45.913
This time

463
32:46.830 --> 32:48.905
you're not getting away.

464
32:49.048 --> 32:50.048
Go!

465
32:57.733 --> 32:58.143
Hey.

466
32:58.680 --> 32:59.842
Where did he go?

467
33:01.317 --> 33:02.317
Hey.

468
33:06.665 --> 33:07.665
Nam.

469
33:13.401 --> 33:14.401
Hey.

470
33:15.288 --> 33:16.750
You're under arrest!

471
33:16.878 --> 33:17.481
Don't.

472
33:17.808 --> 33:18.808
A ghost!

473
33:19.480 --> 33:20.640
I need to take the money too.

474
33:20.691 --> 33:22.424
Hey. Help.

475
33:22.646 --> 33:23.646
Hey. Open up.

476
33:23.851 --> 33:25.430
Who locked the door? Open it.

477
33:27.090 --> 33:27.666
Rule number eight.

478
33:27.691 --> 33:29.972
Store property must not be taken for personal use

479
33:29.997 --> 33:31.949
or embezzled under any circumstances.

480
33:53.303 --> 33:54.455
I'll call an ambulance.

481
33:55.735 --> 33:56.735
Don't, Dear.

482
33:57.027 --> 33:58.027
Why not?

483
33:58.750 --> 33:59.769
We can call one first.

484
33:59.950 --> 34:00.410
I think there's still time.

485
34:00.435 --> 34:01.435
Dear.

486
34:08.422 --> 34:09.422
Don't.

487
34:14.022 --> 34:15.379
Why didn't you save me?

488
34:18.489 --> 34:19.956
Why did you let me die?

489
34:27.369 --> 34:28.369
Hey.

490
34:29.033 --> 34:30.233
What are you sitting here for?

491
34:32.017 --> 34:33.879
I'm gathering evidence on that Pruek guy.

492
34:34.156 --> 34:35.156
I'll help you, Nam.

493
34:40.033 --> 34:41.033
Mom.

494
34:44.314 --> 34:46.159
Are you going to let Metha die?

495
34:46.282 --> 34:48.783
Business investments always carry risks, Officer.

496
34:49.110 --> 34:50.262
Metha.

497
34:50.324 --> 34:51.324
Don't answer her.
